  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1029 PM CDT Thu May 7 2026\n\nBy Sunday, a longwave trough sets up over the eastern CONUS, and a \ncold front will approach from the west. This gives medium to high \nrain chances Sunday afternoon into early Monday. Moisture values \nwill be on the rise, but PWATs aren't that impressive with models \nshowing around an inch or a little over which is near normal for the \ntime of the year. As such, forecast rain amounts also aren't that \nimpressive at generally less than 0.25 inches, and the probability \nof exceeding this at only 30-40%. Some good news though is \nconditions don't look favorable for severe weather.\n\nThe cold front pushes through the area by Monday morning, and drier, \ncooler air moves in behind it. High temperatures on Monday fall back \ninto the upper-60s to low-70s, but will gradually warm back up to \nnear 80 thereafter. Another disturbance clips the area late Tuesday \ninto Wednesday, giving a low chance for another round of rain, but \nstill, nothing hazardous looks to be upcoming.",
